1. PROJECT INFORMATION

Project:
BKAI – Concrete Crack Segmentation and
Skeleton-Based Geometric Characterization

Research publication:
An integrated mask R-CNN framework for concrete crack
segmentation and skeleton-based quantification in
automated infrastructure inspection.

Authors:
Dat-Thanh Nguyen, Nhat-Quang Tran, Duc-Hoc Tran

Journal:
Journal of Building Pathology and Rehabilitation
Volume 11, Article 228 (2026)
Springer Nature

DOI:
https://doi.org/10.1007/s41024-026-00900-z

Official research repository:
https://github.com/bkai-ndt-sdh231/BKAI-Model-Mask-R-CNN


2. PURPOSE OF THIS REPOSITORY

This repository is maintained to introduce and document
the BKAI Mask R-CNN research framework associated with
the published scientific article.

It may contain research descriptions, selected experimental
results, figures, demonstrations, and supporting materials.

The repository is intended to facilitate research visibility,
academic reference, and technical understanding.

The complete scientific methodology and experimental
discussion are available through the official publication.


